A timer line that fires stays armed.
It would signal again every time the timer looks;
after the timer looks no Irq armed on a timer line is due.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-rp2350 fuzz-smp2 fuzz-work test qemu-replay
Report: armed timer line is due
Witness: fuzz cores-timer-across

diff --git a/kernel/sched.c b/kernel/sched.c
--- a/kernel/sched.c
+++ b/kernel/sched.c
@@ -986,7 +986,7 @@ void sched_time(uint64_t now)
         }
         struct core *armed = &cores[irq->core];
         if (irq_due(irq, now)) {
-            irq_signal(irq);
+            sched_signal(irq_notification(irq), irq->bits);
         } else if (irq->deadline < armed->nearest_deadline) {
             armed->nearest_deadline = irq->deadline;
         }
